*.swp
*~

# Test artifacts
art/__diffs__/
vrt/test-results/
vrt/playwright-report/
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/
# `--reporter=blob` (what the sharded e2e job uses) writes here, so anyone who
# reproduces a shard locally leaves an untracked zip behind. The sibling
# report dirs were ignored; this one was not.
e2e/blob-report/
e2e/vrt/test-results-annotated/
coverage/

# Synthesised test-time artifacts. The registry manifest is emitted by
# packages/web/src/lib/dev/registry-manifest.test.ts on every `task test`
# run and consumed by every Playwright spec that iterates the module
# registry — keep it out of git so PR diffs don't bounce on it.
e2e/.generated/

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
*.log

# Flox keeps its run state local
.flox/run/
.flox/cache/

# Wrangler / Cloudflare local state
.wrangler/
**/.wrangler/

# Local Claude Code settings (per-machine, don't commit)
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**

# Playwright artifacts that aren't already covered above
e2e/.last-run.json
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/

# VRT gallery output — generated by `task vrt:gallery` from
# e2e/vrt/__screenshots__/** + the last test-results/. CI regenerates this
# and uploads to GitHub Pages; never commit it to main.
docs/vrt/
e2e/vrt/report/

# Per-PR VRT changeset gallery (only-the-changed baselines, OLD/NEW/DIFF) —
# generated by scripts/vrt-changeset-gallery.mjs and published per-PR to CF
# Pages by .github/workflows/vrt-changeset-gallery.yml. Never committed.
docs/vrt-changeset/

# ART gallery output — waveform + spectrogram PNGs of every art/baselines/**.f32,
# generated by `art/build_gallery.py`. CI regenerates this and publishes it to
# GitHub Pages (.github/workflows/art-gallery.yml + pages.yml); never commit it.
docs/art/

# Synthesised test-time artifacts (gitignored on PR #224 too)
e2e/.generated/

# Long-lived local single-test server state (PID + logs) created by
# `task e2e:serve` / scripts/dev-server.sh. Per-machine runtime; never commit.
.dev-server/


# Blood game data. WHAT SHIPS IN-REPO AND WHY IS ADR-007 —
# docs/adr/007-game-asset-distribution.md. That ADR is the canonical answer
# (including the open owner decision on the shareware's legal status); do not
# re-argue it here, and do not change these rules without amending it —
# scripts/game-asset-distribution.test.ts asserts the committed set against it.
#
# The broad ignore stays, so a stray FULL-GAME copy or a node-only build
# artifact can't be committed. The 1997 SHAREWARE subset (episode 1) is
# un-ignored FILE BY FILE below — the exact set, never a pattern — so the BLOOD
# card boots out-of-box. The big binaries route to Git LFS via the
# .gitattributes rules for static/blood/*.RFF / *.ART / *.DAT.
packages/web/static/blood/*
!packages/web/static/blood/README.md
!packages/web/static/blood/blood.js
!packages/web/static/blood/blood.wasm
# The blood-pcm AudioWorklet (the live game-audio capture bridge feeding
# audio_l/audio_r). A REQUIRED runtime asset like blood.js — un-ignore it or the
# blanket `static/blood/*` rule above drops it from the commit, so CI's build
# serves no worklet (addModule 404 → audio_l silent) though local dev works.
!packages/web/static/blood/blood-pcm-worklet.js
# Bundled 1997 Blood shareware data (un-ignore the exact shareware set only).
!packages/web/static/blood/BLOOD.RFF
!packages/web/static/blood/GUI.RFF
!packages/web/static/blood/SOUNDS.RFF
!packages/web/static/blood/SURFACE.DAT
!packages/web/static/blood/TABLES.DAT
!packages/web/static/blood/VOXEL.DAT
!packages/web/static/blood/SHARE000.ART
# BLOOD.INI — the shareware episode/level descriptor (plain text, NOT in the RFF;
# the engine aborts without it). Small text file → ordinary git, not LFS.
!packages/web/static/blood/BLOOD.INI

# NBlood upstream scratch checkout fetched by build-blood-wasm.sh (the engine is
# fetched at a pinned commit for the WASM build, NOT vendored in this spike).
packages/web/native/nblood/.upstream/
# Phase-1 link object cache (build-blood-wasm.sh BLOOD_LINK=1).
packages/web/native/nblood/.objcache/

# .myrobots is COMMITTED in this repo (owner decision 2026-07-26): agent plans /
# roundups / owner-decision docs are part of the project record. The user-level
# ~/.gitignore_global still ignores .myrobots/ in OTHER repos; these negations
# override it here (repo .gitignore outranks core.excludesFile).
!.myrobots/
!.myrobots/**

# Agent scratch / generated report trees. These must NEVER be tracked: they
# carry local usernames, absolute paths, session UUIDs and agent identities.
# `private/` was committed once (5 files, on public main) — see the CI denylist
# in scripts/no-scratch-tracked.test.ts, which is the gate, not this file.
/private/
**/scratchpad/
**/gallery-out/
